  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_16f05e7265f643fc9d2c4e5ed9c68753",
      "statement": "All persistence in the extension goes through WXT's `storage.defineItem` with an `area:key` prefix, and the codebase defines exactly six items across two Chrome storage areas: `local:settings`, `local:history` and `local:modelCache` in `chrome.storage.local`, and `session:requests`, `session:panelRequests` and `session:panelUrls` in the memory-only `chrome.storage.session`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/history.ts#L50-L52",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e4368d0de738100bb5d495da6fb1c3eec5f73dc5d5ca3100f14ebb66569e089d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/models.ts#L101-L104",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f0dd6238576258163e1683a6b2e9a6739925fc8623b152415b3eea882d38c3ad:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/pending.ts#L10-L14",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b2465ec87df8d2cec9ffa5eb6b6cd5542474a58d53c94b6528a6325f4a9791a1:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/pending.ts#L51-L58",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:67241f155a0fed9b965e0d8f2644632fd3071bec64907a816dcc38131b4e26f6:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/settings.ts#L217-L220",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:049fd299d9b1612e8c1eb861f8e9da3eaf75a0573d9c6b22a105893e4e5e69ff:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4743d1a93ad9497a98e3edfa40db538d",
      "statement": "The `local:` prefix (rather than `sync:`) is used for the settings item specifically so that the per-provider API keys are never replicated through the user's browser account, and no `sync:` storage item exists anywhere in the codebase.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/settings.ts#L216-L220",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5ad55589df1c9e52ce3d054236e4d81365bfc4782f1e80abe8fc8fe35c5e3f72:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b39b5cf73eac45ab80224b2decb92ca1",
      "statement": "Every provider's API key, base URL and model are kept together in the single `Settings.providers` map inside `local:settings`, so switching providers preserves each provider's key, and the key is written to no other storage area.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/settings.ts#L137-L143",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:16d5d7cbd177e877ec6004fd096848439f233f72b113c02490027408cb6b944a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/settings.ts#L140-L160",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9e064211b32ef7dda530790a89c8fc0123e68d6dd28f44487438617812501733:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5f1995723cb340f0918417918604c01f",
      "statement": "`normalizeSettings()` is the only gate between a raw stored settings blob and the typed `Settings` object: it fills in defaults and discards values from older versions (unknown provider, unknown theme, an invalid `display`, unknown summary styles), so a settings blob written by an earlier version cannot break a newer one.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/settings.ts#L222-L231",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ea4859fc80824e525341cf46aa22850a6177693b0091adc62eb3a918e740f947:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_311730dc6a22487bb0eb54a078f0b2e8",
      "statement": "`components/useSettings.ts` is the single reactive read path for settings: it loads once via `getSettings()` and then keeps the value in sync through `settingsItem.watch`, and it exposes a `loaded` flag that the result view waits for before handling a routed request, because the request needs the provider configuration.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://components/useSettings.ts#L1-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dd8a04b5662d348eec353a87f5a6d6cfad695e99ed93cdae5f7b3f5669f7e5d4:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://entrypoints/app/App.tsx#L106-L125",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:246483d576d6929ce17e4ee84dcaa1760103995e5bddec6ef58103fe62f1cb38:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9914f2d6e63b4f85936eeb31e9ad8cb6",
      "statement": "The background worker watches the settings item and compares `next.display` with `prev.display` to re-sync the toolbar action and the context menus, so switching between tab and sidepanel display mode takes effect without restarting the browser.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://entrypoints/background.ts#L37-L40",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5206e17379713b907e6f01c9573148ccb0985c8814105023302c369a258f6f16:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_159c2a122d3042b1b11ab6749a35e42f",
      "statement": "`local:history` stores at most 20 `Session` objects; `saveSession()` prepends the session, removes any earlier entry with the same id so a re-save replaces rather than duplicates, and truncates the list to the newest 20 entries.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/history.ts#L49-L60",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:25616a724a689de784b3749c46bfd35255e263ed2f61ae228824ece4220936ce:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_027000ccc02a4c2dbbc972ca6e2eec9f",
      "statement": "A session's summary and every Q&A answer are stored as OpenUI Message Protocol payloads written with `buildMessage` and read back with `parseMessage`; the stored payload carries the program in `content`, the renderer's form/`$state` map in `context.formState` and the model's prose note in `context.note`, and the context block is omitted entirely when there is neither a note nor a non-empty form state.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/history.ts#L28-L48",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f3849212d10aad14d694f4de031197759456d8814486cbece918d3ddae2ebe1e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_da5e268ead4848fe8da8c720b0ff80f4",
      "statement": "Only the `content` of a stored message is ever sent back to the model — the protocol markers and the form state never leave the browser in a prompt.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/generate.ts#L125-L129",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6c3fcccf895ac680c11f87701e305976d849cd5ddf43e99dc56171d430ffbb22:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/history.ts#L5-L9",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:73d92a46021879d91c0c746b2b2346888fccb34523b1f4c6c5c024694bd752a7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_71bf17cf80484d2b9aa47f6050dbc893",
      "statement": "A stored message is passed to the OpenUI `Renderer` directly as its `response`, so the renderer can consume the stored payload without a conversion step, and the stored message is tagged with `attributes: { app: 'ai-summarizer@1' }` and an end marker.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://components/GenUI.tsx#L20-L44",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cfd296c50e785a8222e0e3181b4fe3498aa976325301450a0f13922d065870ee:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/history.ts#L40-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cf392bbbe16de38e2ff4df55cd868c4330faeef7cdd4b8179d86bee90178e036:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_475cb4a540074c4798fc5306067f920d",
      "statement": "Renderer form and `$state` changes are persisted into the session payload with a 500 ms debounce: `updateSummaryState` rewrites the summary and `updateAnswerState` rewrites one Q&A turn, and in both cases the in-memory session ref is updated synchronously while only the `saveSession` disk write is debounced.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://components/useSession.ts#L203-L228",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a58c715f5685c1765860ad6cde4c0a0e46efe2de9ed0e7027502f22382272d59:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c6406487752f425e897fce4b93da9368",
      "statement": "Because the persisted form state includes the values of generated filters, the in-browser CSV `toolProvider` (`csv_rows` / `csv_group`) re-renders without a new model call and the same filter is still applied when the session is reopened from history.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://components/SessionView.tsx#L53-L55",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a18afd0eaf470f19de34f62ede3cbb451d66a620f882fc5e6a474fdf52e19ed3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/csv-tools.ts#L1-L35",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6472060a1f4fa8007588a3154ed4c8ee9a9f5ea161e3b044fc91e8a12d023d0a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a656ca1b85274f8a845580751f5e06be",
      "statement": "On reopen, `SessionView` passes the stored `context.formState` back to the renderer as `initialState` and keys the renderer by `session.id`, so form values are hydrated and a previous session's form state cannot leak into the next one.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://components/SessionView.tsx#L140-L148",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5ae38ed3142ccefb58471f4cc5f533bf27a3745bfaf0464b82417cbccfd1e20d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://components/SessionView.tsx#L276-L295",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5d95cb8a9975ce5a988857236984af81ad2f1c522e55bcdfb90b7e9fa284e240:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_28c710db2d81473bac4634953d153dae",
      "statement": "`useSession` commits the session to history after every turn — when it is created, when a summary arrives, when a refinement is merged and when an answer is appended — so an interrupted generation still appears in history with its source and a null summary.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://components/useSession.ts#L25-L29",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f104dc2c5746fe488f162f799777a3748920ed35ab14218bd8e25a41f0b02f18:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://components/useSession.ts#L83-L96",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8d6af1f05d158ca8a4f58099997b54e2c842e3388abb06cd9eeccb2c2e1d8d14:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7f6db4c7c9714f73a8e991a7b6f0fa55",
      "statement": "Reopening a session that was saved without a summary triggers a fresh summary run for that source, so a session interrupted by a closed tab is completed when it is opened again.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://components/useSession.ts#L231-L243",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1f359867cc6a33a520e35173fb153abfb1a19d17a8f48d23ab58d2078db3942b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_02c669cdd40b4148b7b92961b703636c",
      "statement": "Refinement reads the current program out of the stored message and writes the merged program back with the existing form state preserved and only the note replaced, so a refinement does not discard the persisted renderer state.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://components/useSession.ts#L136-L162",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5a7fa1ef6824f833c15f62f73695dd877c80c63314143ff1d2e7a772bafd8341:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_46dcb56747de4cce9d089ca68f722ea6",
      "statement": "The pending-request handoff lives in `chrome.storage.session` so that large pasted or selected text never travels in a URL and never outlives the browser session; `queueRequest()` assigns a UUID and opportunistically drops entries older than 10 minutes, and `takeRequest()` returns the request once and removes it so reloading the result page does not re-run the summary.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/pending.ts#L1-L33",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c0709559af851f9b3823adf01ab9c69dfc443d5623d2bb8da67ccc641471c449:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f857bdc21de6445f9ebdb1223bc808ef",
      "statement": "`session:panelRequests` holds only a per-tab pointer to a request id, and `takePanelRequest` consumes that pointer and honours it for 60 seconds only; the window exists because `sendToSidePanel` writes the pointer after the panel document has already been opened, so the panel may mount before the entry exists and must poll once and then watch the storage item.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://entrypoints/app/App.tsx#L70-L85",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b016a01ff18147d8f067dc4c66a28c411bd10296753be904700e9b903f57efaa:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/pending.ts#L51-L105",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c4b827c10224a79e848b51b00a926f1481d057fad5145b601542a3f51aef75ac:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6e2829523eeb4c00a61d7564273624ab",
      "statement": "`session:panelUrls` records the URL each tab's panel belongs to so the background worker can close the panel when that tab navigates to a different document; URLs are compared without the fragment, so in-page anchors keep the panel open, and the entry is removed when the panel is closed or the tab is removed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://entrypoints/background.ts#L42-L50",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7a0ca1c4a5a00bd3dadf4aa990f687d44f9b7731bf202e71a42dc996f4908796:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/pending.ts#L56-L62",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:477cb376d7e8219342505e90d4437570f6dec0da0985df1beed43a4a1494d9a2:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/pending.ts#L98-L109",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:95aa3c92f94bf89b8fbe2d9d8af86d5770ca754efe5c70ddfe99ca895cef2e5c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_583c5948a7424ee1801548de8f3915af",
      "statement": "`local:modelCache` stores the last loaded model list per provider so the model picker works without a new request; `SettingsForm.loadModels()` replaces that provider's entry after a successful fetch and `ModelSwitcher` reads the cache through `getValue()` plus a watcher.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://components/ModelSwitcher.tsx#L40-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:96e51c6aea42f96665af38c6f90a8fd273f7416b6e4705fd16d088342df39a5a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://components/SettingsForm.tsx#L137-L147",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:818f2e39bc0282e5eca360866ba7640c32b570fa4a046682731348e4f0670286:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/models.ts#L101-L104",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f0dd6238576258163e1683a6b2e9a6739925fc8623b152415b3eea882d38c3ad:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_26c768a899284bc1b040224744bcf291",
      "statement": "The cached model list also determines whether a keyless provider (Ollama, LM Studio, custom endpoint) counts as connected: `isProviderConnected` accepts either a chosen model or a cached model list, so such a provider shows as connected without further setup.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/models.ts#L106-L115",
